1
00:00:01,433 --> 00:00:02,600
Yeah.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:04,833
Uh-huh, I see.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,900
Are you sure you don't need help?

4
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:10,300
Yeah.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,767
There wasn't much stuff.

6
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:14,667
We finished faster than expected.

7
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,833
I see.

8
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,467
That's good.

9
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:24,500
How's Kamekichi doing?

10
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:31,533
Me?

11
00:00:31,933 --> 00:00:33,700
Maybe the air is better here.

12
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:35,433
He seems to have really settled in.

13
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,200
He looks even more energetic than before.

14
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,467
Really?

15
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:42,700
Ah, but it still depends on
whether Takoi-san is okay with it.

16
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,233
Of course I'm fine with it.

17
00:00:46,367 --> 00:00:50,233
This gives me an excuse
to come over, right?

18
00:00:50,767 --> 00:00:51,833
Huh?

19
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,300
Even if someone sees us,
they won't think it's weird.

20
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:58,467
Got it.

21
00:00:58,733 --> 00:00:59,933
Leave it to me!

22
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:02,933
It's heavy.
Yeah.

23
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:05,233
Whoa.

24
00:01:05,867 --> 00:01:07,367
Okay.

25
00:01:07,467 --> 00:01:09,000
Let's live together.

26
00:01:14,167 --> 00:01:15,467
Nothing much has changed.

27
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:17,867
He seems to be getting
used to my room, too.

28
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:20,400
I see.

29
00:01:20,733 --> 00:01:22,067
That's good.

30
00:01:24,067 --> 00:01:25,600
Though it's a bit lonely.

31
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,167
You like it better here,
don't you, Kamekichi?

32
00:01:31,267 --> 00:01:33,333
Do you miss Shiono?

33
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:40,367
Ah, I heard it's going
to be sunny on Sunday.

34
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:43,500
Oh, really?

35
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:44,600
Yeah.

36
00:01:44,633 --> 00:01:45,833
That's great.

37
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,160
If we're going to the beach,
it definitely has to be sunny.

38
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,833
I wouldn't mind if it rained.

39
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:53,833
Hmm?

40
00:01:53,933 --> 00:01:56,200
As long as it's a date with Takoi-san,

41
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:57,767
I'll be happy no matter what.

42
00:02:00,667 --> 00:02:04,633
Well... I feel the same way.

43
00:02:04,967 --> 00:02:06,133
Huh?

44
00:02:06,233 --> 00:02:07,500
I can't hear you.

45
00:02:08,067 --> 00:02:09,367
I feel the same way!

46
00:02:09,467 --> 00:02:10,967
Huh? What did you say?

47
00:02:11,067 --> 00:02:12,100
Huh?

48
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:14,500
I said I'm really happy too!

49
00:02:15,433 --> 00:02:17,533
The signal is bad. I can't hear you.

50
00:02:17,633 --> 00:02:18,833
You little...

51
00:02:18,933 --> 00:02:19,933
I said I'm really happy.

52
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,333
Stop making me repeat it.

53
00:02:24,267 --> 00:02:25,667
I'm really looking forward to it.

54
00:02:26,633 --> 00:02:27,800
Yeah.

55
00:02:30,133 --> 00:02:31,400
Good morning.

56
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:32,800
Morning!

57
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:35,967
Good morning.

58
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:38,967
Morning!

59
00:02:39,067 --> 00:02:40,167
Morning.

60
00:02:41,333 --> 00:02:42,600
Huh?

61
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:43,833
Ah.

62
00:02:43,933 --> 00:02:46,433
You seem to be in a great mood.

63
00:02:46,533 --> 00:02:47,667
It's nothing, really.

64
00:02:47,767 --> 00:02:48,367
What's up? What's going on?

65
00:02:48,467 --> 00:02:49,476
- What's up?
- It's nothing.

66
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:51,233
Morning, Takoi.

67
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:52,133
Morning.

68
00:02:52,233 --> 00:02:53,800
What's going on? Do you know something?

69
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,200
Good morning, everyone.

70
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,200
Morning...

71
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:57,633
Looks like everyone is here.

72
00:02:57,733 --> 00:02:59,467
I have someone to introduce to you all.

73
00:02:59,567 --> 00:03:00,833
Come on in.

74
00:03:04,433 --> 00:03:07,567
He's replacing Shiono in the
Community Safety Division.

75
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:08,833
Omaeda.

76
00:03:09,867 --> 00:03:12,800
I'm Omaeda, assigned to the
Yama-no-michi Police Station.

77
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:14,233
Nice to meet you all.

78
00:03:14,933 --> 00:03:15,667
I'm Takoi.

79
00:03:15,767 --> 00:03:16,767
I'm Hasegawa.

80
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:18,100
I'm Egawa.

81
00:03:19,133 --> 00:03:22,467
Even though Omaeda is assigned
to the Community Safety Division,

82
00:03:22,567 --> 00:03:25,700
the chief asked us to
show him around the station.

83
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,433
Huh? We have to do it?

84
00:03:27,533 --> 00:03:29,467
It seems they're short-handed over there.

85
00:03:29,867 --> 00:03:32,667
Do they think the Criminal
Affairs Division has nothing to do?

86
00:03:32,767 --> 00:03:34,200
Yeah, seriously.

87
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:38,467
I heard from the chief that everyone
in the Criminal Affairs Division is elite.

88
00:03:38,567 --> 00:03:40,100
Thanks to all of you,

89
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,967
the public order here is so good.

90
00:03:43,033 --> 00:03:44,300
Oh?

91
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,800
Well, I guess you could say that.

92
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,200
Yeah.

93
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:49,767
Alright, Takoi.

94
00:03:49,867 --> 00:03:50,500
You show him the ropes.

95
00:03:50,767 --> 00:03:52,400
Huh? Me?

96
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:56,067
They said to ask Takoi-san
if I have any questions.

97
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:59,733
I heard you're a very popular detective.

98
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:01,800
Ah, well...

99
00:04:03,567 --> 00:04:04,733
Of course, no problem.

100
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:05,900
What was that about?

101
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,600
Alright then, Omaeda.

102
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,700
I'm counting on you.

103
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,267
Okay, let's go.

104
00:04:10,367 --> 00:04:12,433
Take care!

105
00:04:38,467 --> 00:04:41,800
"Duty First, Kiss Later"

106
00:04:42,733 --> 00:04:44,333
(Episode 7)

107
00:04:44,433 --> 00:04:45,567
Okay.

108
00:04:45,667 --> 00:04:46,667
Thank you.

109
00:04:50,233 --> 00:04:52,533
Alright, OK.

110
00:04:52,733 --> 00:04:55,867
You must always return the
conference room key after using it.

111
00:04:55,967 --> 00:04:57,543
Because there's a guy who loves to nag.

112
00:04:57,567 --> 00:04:58,667
Got it.

113
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,767
That pretty much covers the tour.

114
00:05:04,567 --> 00:05:06,233
I didn't expect you to be so old-school.

115
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:07,200
Really?
Yeah.

116
00:05:07,867 --> 00:05:09,787
I remember things better
when I write them down.

117
00:05:09,833 --> 00:05:11,100
Oh.

118
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:15,076
You were in the Cybercrime
Countermeasures Division before, right?

119
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,233
Yes.

120
00:05:16,333 --> 00:05:18,333
But only for a short while.

121
00:05:18,433 --> 00:05:20,167
It was basically just training.

122
00:05:20,267 --> 00:05:22,467
Still, that's pretty impressive.

123
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:25,433
Omaeda, you're on the
elite track, aren't you?

124
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:28,667
You'll probably be transferred to HQ soon.

125
00:05:28,767 --> 00:05:30,167
I wouldn't know about that.

126
00:05:30,267 --> 00:05:31,967
I still have a long way to go.

127
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:34,333
It's a rare opportunity.

128
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:37,367
Work hard and aim for an early promotion.

129
00:05:37,467 --> 00:05:38,787
Let me know if you need anything.

130
00:05:39,667 --> 00:05:40,933
- Okay.
- By the way,

131
00:05:41,033 --> 00:05:43,400
pull some strings for me someday, will you?

132
00:05:44,867 --> 00:05:45,400
I'll do my best.
Oh.

133
00:05:46,433 --> 00:05:47,867
I'm looking forward to it.

134
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:51,967
Omaeda seems like a sharp guy.

135
00:05:52,067 --> 00:05:52,867
Yeah.

136
00:05:52,967 --> 00:05:54,833
And very earnest, too.

137
00:05:55,267 --> 00:05:56,500
Oh man.

138
00:05:56,833 --> 00:05:57,567
It's scary.

139
00:05:57,667 --> 00:05:59,076
He's exactly like me when I was young.

140
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:00,233
Give me a break.

141
00:06:01,167 --> 00:06:02,800
Time to eat!

142
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:07,167
So hot...

143
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:08,667
Takoi.

144
00:06:08,767 --> 00:06:10,167
Can't you eat properly?

145
00:06:10,267 --> 00:06:11,667
I'm perfectly calm.

146
00:06:11,767 --> 00:06:12,333
Careful, it's hot.

147
00:06:12,433 --> 00:06:13,433
By the way,

148
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:14,940
didn't something good happen to you?

149
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,833
What exactly happened? Spill it.

150
00:06:17,933 --> 00:06:19,167
Huh? You don't know?

151
00:06:19,267 --> 00:06:19,867
No clue at all.

152
00:06:19,967 --> 00:06:20,967
- Huh?
- What?

153
00:06:22,033 --> 00:06:24,200
It's not really something
I can tell others...

154
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:27,367
Huh?

155
00:06:27,933 --> 00:06:29,567
Stop keeping us in suspense.

156
00:06:29,667 --> 00:06:32,733
No, really... Well,
maybe just a little bit.

157
00:06:32,833 --> 00:06:33,433
You're dying to tell us, aren't you?

158
00:06:33,533 --> 00:06:34,533
Tell us.

159
00:06:34,767 --> 00:06:35,809
You can't hold it in, can you?

160
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:36,633
Yeah.

161
00:06:36,733 --> 00:06:37,900
Come on, tell us!

162
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:40,633
What is it already?

163
00:06:41,533 --> 00:06:42,933
[From Shiono:] I'm sorry.

164
00:06:43,033 --> 00:06:46,433
Something came up with my family on Sunday.

165
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,400
Huh?!

166
00:06:49,467 --> 00:06:50,800
Ah...

167
00:06:56,933 --> 00:06:59,233
So that's how it is.

168
00:06:59,333 --> 00:07:00,733
What's wrong? Are you okay?

169
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:04,333
Family is definitely important.

170
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,067
Family comes first.

171
00:07:07,633 --> 00:07:10,667
You should just say, "I'm lonely."

172
00:07:10,767 --> 00:07:14,067
You should just say, "I want to see you."

173
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:19,933
You should just say, "I can't eat."

174
00:07:20,033 --> 00:07:21,367
I'll take one then.

175
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,300
Can't eat this yet, it's too hot.

176
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,333
Mmm, so good.

177
00:07:28,433 --> 00:07:29,533
Delicious.

178
00:07:32,267 --> 00:07:36,833
Sigh, it can't be helped.

179
00:07:36,933 --> 00:07:38,933
You have to cherish your family.

180
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:41,033
Sigh.

181
00:07:41,133 --> 00:07:42,700
Shiono...

182
00:07:44,467 --> 00:07:46,587
So this is what a
long-distance relationship is like.

183
00:07:47,033 --> 00:07:48,533
It really is far.

184
00:07:52,133 --> 00:07:53,400
Oh, welcome.

185
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:56,467
Two hours one way, four hours round trip?

186
00:07:57,767 --> 00:08:00,033
If only I could teleport there instantly.

187
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:03,567
That's impossible, of course.

188
00:08:03,667 --> 00:08:05,733
Yeah, of course it's impossible...

189
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:13,067
Huh? Why?

190
00:08:14,067 --> 00:08:16,067
Because you texted me
saying you were drinking.

191
00:08:16,167 --> 00:08:18,500
Huh? So you just came all the way here?

192
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,200
Huh? Do you have tomorrow off?

193
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:21,900
No, I have work.

194
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,133
I'll head back after I eat.

195
00:08:23,233 --> 00:08:24,700
Huh? You're going back from here?

196
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,300
Another two-hour ride?

197
00:08:27,233 --> 00:08:28,567
Is that a problem?

198
00:08:28,667 --> 00:08:31,400
Not exactly a problem...

199
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:32,900
Aren't you exhausted?

200
00:08:32,933 --> 00:08:34,493
Not at all.

201
00:08:36,233 --> 00:08:38,400
I just couldn't stand not
seeing you, Takoi-san.

202
00:08:49,733 --> 00:08:50,933
Here you go.

203
00:08:51,033 --> 00:08:52,233
Thanks.

204
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:54,300
Well then...

205
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:55,900
Oh.

206
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:04,947
You know, you could've given
me a heads-up before coming.

207
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:06,800
I thought you liked surprises.

208
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,733
Not even a little.

209
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:22,667
Sigh... No matter how exhausted
I am, I always crave a drink.

210
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,300
You should just drink less.

211
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:27,233
I can't help it.

212
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:30,400
A drink today
gives me the fuel to keep working tomorrow.

213
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,133
Is that so?

214
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:40,400
Shiono, can you catch your train?

215
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,500
Yeah, I have plenty of time.

216
00:09:44,533 --> 00:09:46,100
Oh, I see...

217
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:54,867
Isn't it about time we changed
how we address each other?

218
00:09:55,133 --> 00:09:56,133
Huh?

219
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:01,167
Stop calling me "Shiono."

220
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:03,333
Use my first name.

221
00:10:05,067 --> 00:10:06,467
Ah...

222
00:10:07,167 --> 00:10:08,167
Uh...

223
00:10:08,267 --> 00:10:09,267
Shu...

224
00:10:12,233 --> 00:10:13,500
Shu.

225
00:10:19,467 --> 00:10:20,667
Not bad.

226
00:10:23,933 --> 00:10:27,267
Do you want to stay the night?

227
00:10:30,367 --> 00:10:31,667
No.

228
00:10:31,767 --> 00:10:33,267
I'll head back today.

229
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:35,933
Oh... I see.

230
00:10:41,167 --> 00:10:42,167
Takoi-san.

231
00:10:42,267 --> 00:10:43,433
Yeah?

232
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,600
Next time I visit, I'll stay the night.

233
00:10:59,733 --> 00:11:00,900
Okay.

234
00:11:17,933 --> 00:11:20,233
(Yama-no-michi Police Station)

235
00:11:35,367 --> 00:11:36,809
- The inspectors are here.
- How many of them?

236
00:11:36,833 --> 00:11:37,467
I don't know.

237
00:11:37,567 --> 00:11:39,233
The inspectors are here.

238
00:11:39,667 --> 00:11:41,100
The inspectors have arrived.

239
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,267
Inspectors?

240
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Huh?

241
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,000
Hmm?

242
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:55,209
What's going on? What's happening?

243
00:11:55,233 --> 00:11:56,400
Huh?

244
00:11:59,167 --> 00:12:01,567
Wait, isn't that Shiono?

245
00:12:01,667 --> 00:12:03,233
What are people from HQ doing here?

246
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:05,700
Shiono!

247
00:12:07,967 --> 00:12:09,067
What the heck?

248
00:12:09,167 --> 00:12:11,076
You could've at least
told me you were coming...

249
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,433
Long time no see.

250
00:12:12,533 --> 00:12:13,667
Huh?

251
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,733
Excuse me.

252
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:37,800
Are you Chief Takoi?

253
00:12:38,267 --> 00:12:39,300
Yes.

254
00:12:40,267 --> 00:12:42,367
Hmm...

255
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,367
I see.

256
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:45,900
Huh?

257
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:50,167
I've heard about you
from Squad Leader Shiono.

258
00:12:50,267 --> 00:12:52,000
I've been looking forward to meeting you.

259
00:12:52,967 --> 00:12:54,267
Oh...

260
00:12:54,367 --> 00:12:57,467
I'm Date, the inspector
in charge of this case.

261
00:12:57,567 --> 00:12:58,667
Nice to meet you.

262
00:13:03,233 --> 00:13:04,233
Nice to meet you too.

263
00:13:04,267 --> 00:13:07,300
Eek!

264
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:17,067
I hear you've been taking
good care of our Shu.

265
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,533
What?

266
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:20,633
George-san.

267
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:22,567
Okay, I'm coming.

268
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,733
Please excuse me.

269
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,167
Shu?

270
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,800
George-san?

271
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,933
I heard they're inspectors.

272
00:13:44,033 --> 00:13:44,533
Inspectors?
Yes.

273
00:13:45,233 --> 00:13:48,733
Word is, internal data leaked
from a police station in the prefecture.

274
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:49,700
Really?

275
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:52,800
So it seems they're
investigating other stations too.

276
00:13:53,567 --> 00:13:55,167
Since we've got so much free time,

277
00:13:55,267 --> 00:13:57,367
we might get called in for backup.

278
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:05,200
Aren't you happy?

279
00:14:05,933 --> 00:14:08,400
It's not every day you get to
see Shiono on the job, right?

280
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:09,667
This is a rare opportunity.

281
00:14:09,767 --> 00:14:10,100
Hey, you guys.
Hey!

282
00:14:11,033 --> 00:14:12,176
- What's with the "hey"?
- What do you say?

283
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:12,833
- Stop messing around.
- Hey.
Yes.

284
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:16,300
Come to the conference room later.

285
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:18,067
- Hmm?
- Huh?!

286
00:14:18,167 --> 00:14:19,467
You come too.

287
00:14:21,133 --> 00:14:22,300
Yes, sir.

288
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:27,300
What is this?

289
00:14:28,233 --> 00:14:32,900
Chief Takoi made this.

290
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:38,100
Excuse me.

291
00:14:39,667 --> 00:14:40,667
Chief Takoi.

292
00:14:40,733 --> 00:14:41,733
Yes.

293
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,100
What is this?

294
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:45,500
Huh?

295
00:14:46,833 --> 00:14:49,333
It's just a common communication error.

296
00:14:49,433 --> 00:14:50,900
It's not a problem.

297
00:14:52,533 --> 00:14:53,800
I see.

298
00:14:54,633 --> 00:14:56,433
What about the other parts?

299
00:14:57,433 --> 00:14:58,600
Hmm?

300
00:15:02,367 --> 00:15:03,600
Hmm?

301
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:11,867
Hmm...?

302
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:14,733
Looking at this data so far,

303
00:15:14,833 --> 00:15:17,433
there doesn't seem to be anything unusual.

304
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,700
Huh?

305
00:15:29,067 --> 00:15:31,600
Who made report number 273?

306
00:15:36,867 --> 00:15:38,100
I did.

307
00:15:40,567 --> 00:15:41,800
What's wrong?

308
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:43,267
Look here.

309
00:15:48,167 --> 00:15:50,667
Right before this,
some weird code popped up.

310
00:15:51,167 --> 00:15:53,867
Looks like even the
IP address got hijacked.

311
00:15:53,967 --> 00:15:54,967
What?

312
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:57,567
Thank god the access
restrictions kicked in.

313
00:15:57,667 --> 00:15:59,467
The rest of the data wasn't compromised.

314
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:03,167
That was a really close call...

315
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:05,100
Uh...

316
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:09,033
But I just followed the
Cybercrime Division's instructions.

317
00:16:09,133 --> 00:16:10,200
What?

318
00:16:10,533 --> 00:16:12,000
Are you messing with me?

319
00:16:13,833 --> 00:16:15,509
You can't just brush it off
with "I followed instructions"

320
00:16:15,533 --> 00:16:16,776
- and expect to get away with it.
- Hey...

321
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:19,043
- If things went south, it'd be too late.
- Alright, alright.

322
00:16:19,067 --> 00:16:20,067
But...

323
00:16:20,133 --> 00:16:22,333
Omaeda just transferred here.

324
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:24,967
He probably didn't do it on purpose...

325
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:30,533
That's what I think...

326
00:16:32,467 --> 00:16:35,167
Your name is Omaeda... right?

327
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:38,433
If you're going to be this sloppy,

328
00:16:39,433 --> 00:16:42,033
hand in your badge and go home right now.

329
00:16:50,967 --> 00:16:52,033
Shu!

330
00:16:52,133 --> 00:16:54,233
- What?
- Alright, that's enough.

331
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:01,767
Still, making a mistake isn't exactly
something to be proud of.

332
00:17:03,333 --> 00:17:04,767
Don't let it happen again.

333
00:17:07,667 --> 00:17:08,833
Yes, sir.

334
00:17:11,833 --> 00:17:15,800
So stay sharp
and finish the rest of the checks.

335
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:16,933
Yes, sir!

336
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:20,433
Come on, don't be so down.

337
00:17:22,667 --> 00:17:24,167
I'm sorry.

338
00:17:24,467 --> 00:17:25,233
I...

339
00:17:25,333 --> 00:17:26,973
They're just doing their jobs, after all.

340
00:17:27,767 --> 00:17:28,833
Okay.

341
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,876
I know you just transferred
and it's a lot to take in.

342
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,200
Just be careful next time.

343
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:52,967
We'll head back now.
We'll leave the rest to you.

344
00:17:54,667 --> 00:17:58,167
Shiono... Squad Leader.

345
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:04,967
I'll go on ahead.

346
00:18:15,767 --> 00:18:17,167
What is it?

347
00:18:17,633 --> 00:18:18,833
Ah, well...

348
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:24,533
I'm busy, so make it quick.

349
00:18:26,633 --> 00:18:28,033
Oh...

350
00:18:32,233 --> 00:18:35,233
Don't make that face.

351
00:18:36,067 --> 00:18:37,300
Huh?

352
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:40,700
I was trying so hard to keep my cool.

353
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:42,333
And then you make a face like that.

354
00:18:43,167 --> 00:18:44,867
Now you're making it hard for me to leave.

355
00:18:48,767 --> 00:18:50,800
When you're not so tired,

356
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:52,267
I'll come stay the night.

357
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:58,300
I'll be taking my leave now.

358
00:19:15,933 --> 00:19:18,067
Yes!

359
00:19:20,867 --> 00:19:22,233
Not that way, this way.

360
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:30,600
What's wrong?

361
00:19:30,867 --> 00:19:31,867
No...

362
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,500
- It's nothing.
- Oh, really?

363
00:19:33,933 --> 00:19:36,133
Do you want to come to my place for dinner?

364
00:19:36,433 --> 00:19:37,667
Not today.

365
00:19:37,767 --> 00:19:38,967
Aw, what a shame.

366
00:19:39,067 --> 00:19:40,667
I wanted to eat with you.

367
00:19:44,167 --> 00:19:46,467
Still, Takoi really
exceeded my expectations.

368
00:19:46,567 --> 00:19:47,600
Huh?

369
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:48,943
You don't think he was jealous, do you?

370
00:19:48,967 --> 00:19:50,200
Jealous of me and Shu.

371
00:19:51,733 --> 00:19:54,700
It's pretty cold of him
not to even remember me.

372
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:56,000
You guys knew each other?

373
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,267
Huh?

374
00:19:57,367 --> 00:19:58,533
You didn't know?

375
00:19:59,033 --> 00:20:03,033
But that was a long time ago,
way before I met you.

376
00:20:05,867 --> 00:20:08,300
Hehe...

377
00:20:13,733 --> 00:20:15,167
What the hell?

378
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:17,900
What?

379
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,533
Because it's the first time
I've seen you make that face.

380
00:20:22,333 --> 00:20:23,433
Really?

381
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,433
Did something good happen?

382
00:20:26,033 --> 00:20:27,400
Hmm?

383
00:20:27,933 --> 00:20:30,033
Who knows?

384
00:20:31,833 --> 00:20:33,000
Welcome.

385
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:35,267
Huh? What are you doing here?

386
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:36,567
Hello.

387
00:20:40,433 --> 00:20:43,367
Hasegawa-san told me
you often come here to drink.

388
00:20:43,467 --> 00:20:44,567
Yeah.

389
00:20:44,667 --> 00:20:45,800
Mind if I join you?

390
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:47,300
Not at all, please.

391
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:49,033
Thanks.

392
00:20:50,067 --> 00:20:53,767
This izakaya has a really great vibe.

393
00:20:53,867 --> 00:20:55,100
Thanks.

394
00:20:56,133 --> 00:20:58,267
I'll have a beer then.

395
00:20:59,767 --> 00:21:00,900
What do you want to eat?

396
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:04,767
Though they don't exactly
have any signature dishes here.

397
00:21:04,867 --> 00:21:05,767
Hey!

398
00:21:05,867 --> 00:21:07,133
No, no, I'm kidding.

399
00:21:07,233 --> 00:21:09,667
Don't we have
charcoal-grilled chicken skewers?

400
00:21:09,767 --> 00:21:11,109
Isn't it just meat from the supermarket?

401
00:21:11,133 --> 00:21:11,900
It's not from the supermarket.

402
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,776
It's grilled over charcoal,
smells great, right?

403
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,567
And it's top-grade chicken from Miyagi.

404
00:21:15,667 --> 00:21:16,767
Are you for real?

405
00:21:16,867 --> 00:21:19,076
You're so wasted, you wouldn't
even be able to taste the difference.

406
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:19,900
That's not true.

407
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,543
Last time you even mistook
the shishito peppers for...

408
00:21:21,567 --> 00:21:25,200
(Yama-no-michi Police Station)

409
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:29,433
- Hmm?
- Good morning.

410
00:21:30,133 --> 00:21:31,800
It's probably best to let him know.

411
00:21:32,067 --> 00:21:33,367
Huh? This is...

412
00:21:33,467 --> 00:21:34,300
Yeah...

413
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:35,833
Morning!

414
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:37,933
- Morning...
- Good morning.

415
00:21:39,033 --> 00:21:40,167
What's up?

416
00:21:40,833 --> 00:21:42,567
Can I borrow you for a second?

417
00:21:42,967 --> 00:21:43,633
Hmm?

418
00:21:43,733 --> 00:21:46,173
Well, I found something this morning
that's been bothering me.

419
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,233
Yeah?

420
00:21:47,533 --> 00:21:52,067
It's the account for Mr. Date's dog.

421
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:55,000
Huh?!

422
00:21:55,800 --> 00:22:00,433
(13 hours ago)
(Post) Went to the dog run on Sunday.

423
00:22:01,167 --> 00:22:04,633
Sunday was the day he canceled our date...

424
00:22:12,967 --> 00:22:14,100
Shiono...

425
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,200
Why...

426
00:22:24,867 --> 00:22:27,633
(This drama is a work of fiction)

427
00:22:28,100 --> 00:22:30,460
(Next Episode)
You're being completely strung along.

428
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:32,233
Looks like trouble is brewing.

429
00:22:32,333 --> 00:22:33,813
Don't tell me it's your ex-boyfriend?

430
00:22:34,133 --> 00:22:36,800
All sorts of things...

431
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:37,733
Damn it...

432
00:22:37,833 --> 00:22:40,567
I have no intention of
giving him up to you!

433
00:22:40,667 --> 00:22:41,133
Interesting.

434
00:22:41,233 --> 00:22:43,267
Let's settle this man to man.

435
00:22:43,467 --> 00:22:45,533
Let's go on an overnight trip.

436
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:47,200
Sound good?
